KZ3 patch 2051 (RSX pass 54): RSX_PERF_GPU=1 measures GPU busy time and vertex-fetch time per source type.

Every submit notes its QPC time under its fence value; a 1 ms poller of the fence turns completions into
busy intervals and logs `[perf-gpu] t=Ns lists N busy X ms of Y longest Z`. Default off, no cost when off
(one cached getenv). Used to tell GPU-bound walker waits from latency.

Also times rsx_vertex_fetch_many per NV4097 vertex type (`[perf-vtxtype]`, same switch).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): vertex-profile VP_BEGIN/VP_END hooks in 2040's fetch_many dropped with it (upstream's fetch_many has none; the [vtx-prof] type buckets for the batched path are gone).

